  <page_number>103</page_number>
  <running_head>LYRICA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>G 4</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p><i>Quod portenta truci robore stipitis</i></p>
    <p><i>Olim plurima contudit</i></p>
    <p><i>Et ferro, &amp; rutilis perdidit ignibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Lernea colubros fera</i></p>
    <p><i>Infames: domitis atque latronibus,</i></p>
    <p><i>Immanique Tyrannide</i></p>
    <p><i>Pressa frugiferas reddidit urbibus</i></p>
    <p><i>Paces fortia noxia</i></p>
    <p><i>Imponens potior frena licentia.</i></p>
    <p><i>Laudat postera Theseum</i></p>
    <p><i>Semper fama recens, Dædale domus</i></p>
    <p><i>Audax quod penetrauerit</i></p>
    <p><i>Obscuros aditus, cacaque limina:</i></p>
    <p><i>Atque infamis adultera</i></p>
    <p><i>Partum Pasiphaes presserit Atticis</i></p>
    <p><i>Impositum perimens iugum.</i></p>
    <p><i>Et mandata Ducis tristia Cretici.</i></p>
    <p><i>Sed laus nobilior manet</i></p>
    <p><i>Celsis stelliferi verticibus poli:</i></p>
    <p><i>Qui fortes vitium obruunt:</i></p>
    <p><i>Qui Ditis resecant Tartarei dolos</i></p>
    <p><i>Et mendacia, quo decens</i></p>
    <p><i>Reddatur supero gloria Numini.</i></p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Printer's ornament below the text, not transcribed. Some letters in the long lines are worn (e.g. "Pasiphaes", "cæcaque") and are read from the scan as best possible. The Greek-style ornament and the faint show-through from the reverse page are omitted.</notes>
</page>
